notes               = "Untitled in source. Rhymed on -ا شدم (دوتا شدم / هزارپا شدم / جدا شدم). دوتا شدن is to bend double; هزارپا is a millipede — he grows a thousand feet chasing the moment and still misses it. The last line's آنِ دل sets آن, the instant, against آن meaning grace or charm, and answers the لحظه of the first line. Bare year ۱۳۸۴ → +621 = 2005. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

لحظه با شتاب
از کنار من گذشت
من پی گرفتنش دوتا شدم
بی‌خبر ز حالِ دل
یکسره دویدم و هزارپا شدم
در هوایِ هفته‌هایِ رفته‌ام
از صفای آنِ دل جدا شدم.
تهران ۱۳۸۴

===machine===

The moment went past me
in a hurry.
Chasing it down, I bent double;
knowing nothing of how my heart was,
I ran flat out and turned into a millipede.
In the air of my weeks that are gone
I was cut off from the clearness of that heart's instant.
Tehran 1384

===lantern===

The moment went past me
in a hurry.
Chasing it down, I bent double;
knowing nothing of how my heart was,
I ran flat out and turned into a millipede.
In the air of my weeks that are gone
I was cut off from the clearness of that heart's instant.

Tehran 1384

===translation===

===footnotes===

آن is at once *the instant* and *grace* — the quality that makes a face or a gesture
compelling. The poem spends six lines chasing a moment and loses, in the last line, the other thing
the word means.
